## Markdown versions of every page

Every page here has a plain-Markdown twin at a sibling URL: the same words with
no navigation, styling or scripts, served as `text/markdown`. Twins are `noindex`
— the HTML page stays canonical, and is the URL to cite.

Two rules generate every twin URL:

1. A hand-built page is prefixed with `/md`:
   `/` → `/md/` · `/pricing/` → `/md/pricing/` · `/tools/roi-calculator/` → `/md/tools/roi-calculator/`
2. A collection puts `md` immediately after its section:
   `/blog/{slug}/` → `/blog/md/{slug}/`
   `/blog/` and `/blog/page/{n}/` → `/blog/md/` and `/blog/md/page/{n}/`
   `/blog/app-collections/{slug}/` → `/blog/app-collections/md/{slug}/`
   `/category/{parent}/{child}/` → `/category/md/{parent}/{child}/` (+ `page/{n}/`)
   `/authors/{slug}/` → `/authors/md/{slug}/`
   `/collections/{type}/` → `/collections/md/{type}/` (+ `page/{n}/`)
   `/tools/slogan-generator/{slug}/` → `/tools/slogan-generator/md/{slug}/`

Every page also declares its twin in `<head>`:
`<link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="...">`. If a twin URL 404s, the
page has none — read the HTML page instead.
